WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.839 --> 00:00:11.120
The Council held its monthly meeting for August yesterday.

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:15.539
The first item on the agenda, marked a milestone
for the district’s earthquake recovery,

00:00:15.539 --> 00:00:19.619
as the Earthquake Infrastructure Recovery
Programme delivered its final report.

00:00:19.619 --> 00:00:25.340
48 of the 52 projects in the programme have
been completed, with two more finishing over

00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:27.260
the next couple of months.

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:32.050
The final projects will be undertaken as part
of the Kaiapoi East Regeneration Reserve.

00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:37.510
Not only is the work now essentially completed
- it’s also come in under budget, with approximately

00:00:37.510 --> 00:00:39.480
$400,000 remaining.

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:47.120
Councillors also approved public consultation
around Earthquake Prone Priority Buildings.

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:52.210
Under the Building (Earthquake Prone Buildings)
Amendment Act 2016, the Council must work

00:00:52.210 --> 00:00:56.640
with community to identify earthquake buildings
that are high risk, and should be prioritised

00:00:56.640 --> 00:00:58.430
for remediation.

00:00:58.430 --> 00:01:02.629
Although there are very few of those buildings
left in the district following previous earthquakes,

00:01:02.629 --> 00:01:06.900
the Council has identified a small number
of priority buildings in Rangiora &amp; Kaiapoi,

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:10.780
and will be seeking the input of residents
to identify others.

00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:13.860
The consultation will open for a month from
the 20th of August.

00:01:14.860 --> 00:01:19.740
Finally, the Council has asked for a proposed
consultation around speed limits in the Rangiora-Woodend

00:01:19.749 --> 00:01:23.889
Road area to be sent to the district’s four
Community Boards for review.

00:01:23.889 --> 00:01:28.590
After the Community Boards have made recommendations, Council staff will present a revised

00:01:28.590 --> 00:01:33.000
proposal to the Council, which is then expected to be released for public consultation.

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:37.980
The next Council meeting will take place on
Tuesday 4th of September.

